-- title:
--   Residues of admissible functions are integral over κ_A[jmath̄ ]
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a natural number $M'\neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ with source the base-changed full modular function field $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F_{\mathrm{full}}(M') =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ and target `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, the subfield of $\kappa_A((t))$ generated over the residue field $\kappa_A$ of $A$ by $j$ and $j_{M'}$ mod $q$; thus $R_0$ supplies a valuation subring of integers, a surjective residue map onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees and orders, and compatibility with $A$. It is assumed ($h_{R_0}$) that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, this image lies in $R_0$.`integers` and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Let $\mathcal A$ be a subring of $\mathbb Q((t))$ whose members are characterised as those $gf$ that lie in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (the subfield of $\mathbb Q((t))$ generated by the divisor expansions of level $M'$), whose coefficientwise image lies in $R_0$.`integers`, and which satisfy: for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, if $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $j$ (the $q$-expansion `jq`) is $\ge 0$ then $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $gf$ is $\ge 0$; and assume $j \in \mathcal A$. The conclusion is that for every $gf$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image lies in $R_0$.`integers` and which lies in $\mathcal A$, and given that the image of `jq` lies in $R_0$.`integers`, the residue $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(gf)$ is integral over the $\kappa_A$-subalgebra of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` generated by $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(j)$.
--
--   This is the integrality step in the reduction of the full-level modular function field modulo a prime $q$ not dividing $M'$: admissible rational functions of level $M'$, i.e. those regular wherever $j$ is, reduce to functions integral over $\kappa_A[\bar\jmath\,]$ on the special fibre of $X_0(M')$. It feeds the construction of an algebra homomorphism out of the full-level function field over $\kappa_A$ in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algHom_modularFunctionFieldFullC_of_ringHom_admissible_of_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algHom_modularFunctionFieldFullC_of_ringHom_admissible_of_prime).
